Third-party notices for ctxprune 0.3.0
=====================================

The ctxprune package (the code in this repository and in the wheel, including the
runtime vendored under ctxprune/_rt/) is released under 0BSD; see LICENSE.

Copied third-party code
-----------------------
None. At the time of the 0.3.0 release no third-party source code is copied into
the package. If that changes, the copied file, its origin, its license and its
copyright notice are listed here.

Not part of this package
------------------------
- Optional dependencies of the `model` extra (`pip install "ctxprune[model]"`):
  onnxruntime, tokenizers and numpy. They are installed separately by your
  package manager and stay under their own licenses.
- The v2 line-scoring model weights used by the `balanced` and `aggressive`
  presets. They are not 0BSD and are not shipped in this package. They are a
  fine-tune of mmBERT-small (MIT) trained on data that includes CC-BY-4.0
  datasets (SWE-rebench-openhands, Nemotron-SWE). Their license and the
  required attributions are on the model's Hugging Face model card.

